From: HSL maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: use typed fallbacks and explicit color LUT presence

Use valid, initialized resources when nullDescriptor is unavailable. Preserve
NV12 conversion identity, image dimensionality, layouts and native failures.
Carry paired LUT presence in a push constant, not a null image mip query.
The inverse-tone-map specialization uses GLSL constant ID 7, not 6.
The HSL-authored fallback helper is hash-pinned by the GNU build overlay.
External memory, synchronization and output capability requirements remain.

